# Specific video-and-generation release DOI.
# The research-paper DOI is separate; resource and paper authorship remain distinct.
# Paper references retain all six authors in the original order.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Cite the paper when using the method. If you use or adapt the generation files, also cite the
  specific software release used.
type: software
title: Supplementary video and generation files for the IECON 2026 paper “Current References for Minimum
  Copper Loss and Torque Ripple in the Full Torque-Speed Range for Symmetrical Six-Phase PMSMs With Nonsinusoidal
  Back-EMF Under an Open-Phase Fault”
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23304581
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23304581
authors:
- family-names: Yepes
  given-names: Alejandro G.
repository-code: https://github.com/agyepes/iecon2026-six-phase-pmsm-opf
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: Supplementary software and visualization material accompanying the IECON 2026 paper. A quasi-steady
  video reconstructs stored phase-dependent current references for a symmetrical six-phase PMSM with phase
  a open. The full H21 LUT, original trajectory and video are preserved, including approximately 0.139%
  current and 0.325% voltage continuous-angle overshoots. Playback time is presentation timing. This resource
  remains separate from the interactive HTML supplement.
keywords:
- IECON 2026
- supplementary video
- video generation
- open-phase fault
- six-phase PMSM
- current references
- full H21 lookup table
